<!-- OVERVIEW: one passage; its words darken as it is read, the shield   -->
<!-- closes when the reader reaches the end                              -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->
<section class="section section--white" aria-labelledby="s1-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="story" data-lit>
      <h2 class="story__title story__title--long rv" id="s1-title">Cybersecurity for Manufacturing Industry: Securing Industrial Systems and Production Operations</h2>

      <div class="story__aside" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ icon("gear", "lg") }}
        <span class="story__rail"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="story__body">
        <p>Industrial cybersecurity demands a clear understanding of how factory equipment and enterprise networks interact. Connected machinery and programmable logic controllers (PLCs) now operate alongside cloud applications and Industrial IoT (IIoT) platforms, creating security dependencies that traditional IT protection may not fully address. A weakness in one component can expose production data or provide unauthorized access to critical industrial systems.</p>
        <p>CipherTrivia brings a security-testing perspective to manufacturing environments, examining how attackers could exploit vulnerabilities across industrial networks and connected applications. Our manufacturing cybersecurity services cover penetration testing and vulnerability assessments as well as network security reviews and application security testing, with a focus on access controls and insecure configurations or weaknesses in IT-OT connectivity.</p>
        <p>By connecting technical findings with operational impact, we help manufacturers prioritize remediation based on the risks identified during testing. These cybersecurity solutions for manufacturing support informed security decisions across smart factories and legacy production environments while helping safeguard intellectual property and reduce exposure to operational disruption.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

